WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.370
The strongest one there is.

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:04.447
The largest lawyer in the courtroom.

00:00:04.447 --> 00:00:09.362
If the Hulk and She-Hulk threw down, which
green goliath would come out on top?

00:00:09.583 --> 00:00:15.380
As we've witnessed through multiple MCU outings,
raw strength does not always determine a winner

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:16.380
in a battle.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.840
Still, it doesn't hurt.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:23.109
Fans are given an idea of how strong She-Hulk
is relative to regular Hulk when the two powerhouses

00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:27.359
go toe-to-toe during the first episode of
"She-Hulk: Attorney at Law."

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:31.789
Bruce Banner, in his Professor Hulk form,
tries to convince his cousin that her new

00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:37.519
powers should be used for the good of the
world, but Jennifer isn't interested in becoming a superhero.

00:00:37.519 --> 00:00:41.199
An argument ensues, and when Jennifer loses
her temper.

00:00:41.199 --> 00:00:46.730
She transforms into She-Hulk and
throws the first punch, initiating her first

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.620
superpowered throwdown.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:53.519
Both Hulks land some big blows during this
fight, with Professor Hulk launching his cousin

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:58.769
through the air and She-Hulk breaking the
Avenger's glasses, which only serves to make

00:00:58.769 --> 00:01:00.489
him even angrier.

00:01:00.489 --> 00:01:04.570
It's entertaining, but it doesn't give any
definitive answers in terms of strength.

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:09.460
She-Hulk is still new to the whole Hulk thing,
and Professor Hulk is clearly holding back.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:14.430
Yet, the scene does show that She-Hulk can
at least hold her own against the Avenger,

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:18.580
matching him blow for blow and hurting him
more than once.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:24.990
She isn't afraid to play a little dirty, stomping
on his foot and even running him over with a car.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:30.310
Sometimes it takes nimbleness, speed, and
balance to gain the upper hand in a fight.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:33.350
Unfortunately for Hulk, he's lacking in this
department.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:38.780
A brute beast, Bruce Banner's alter-ego has
historically relied entirely on his ability

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:41.192
to throw the most brutal punches.

00:01:41.192 --> 00:01:43.181
"And, Hulk.

00:01:44.427 --> 00:01:45.595
Smash."

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:53.980
Though he has been known to jump from building
to building in the past, Hulk is about as

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:57.030
far from Spider-Man as a hero can be.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:02.821
She-Hulk does not gain the same lumbering,
musclebound physique as her cousin when she transforms.

00:02:02.821 --> 00:02:08.670
Her physicality does improve dramatically,
however, which makes for better reflexes and balance.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:12.870
As shown during the first episode of "She-Hulk:
Attorney at Law," she naturally becomes a

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:17.000
skilled acrobat, quickly outdoing her powerful
relative.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:22.150
When the two square up, prepared to battle,
Walters appears much more poised and nimbler

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:24.500
than the bulky and lumbering Hulk.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:29.060
While Banner is a lot faster since his two
personalities merged to become Professor Hulk,

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:32.267
he's nowhere near as nimble as She-Hulk.

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:34.960
Which Hulk has won the most fights?

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:38.970
One would think that this would be no contest
considering Bruce Banner has been smashing

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:41.340
his way through the MCU since 2008.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:46.190
Unfortunately, Hulk's track record in the
MCU is not quite as good as one would expect.

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:51.140
In fact, audiences have witnessed the big
green monster lose more often than not.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:56.110
Hulk was convincingly defeated by Thanos in
"Avengers: Infinity War," and before that

00:02:56.110 --> 00:03:01.590
he got a beatdown courtesy of Tony Stark and
his Hulkbuster suit in "Avengers: Age of Ultron."

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:06.990
There's also his near loss to the titular
God of Thunder in "Thor: Ragnarok" to consider.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:11.970
Hulk hasn't really won a superhuman battle
since throwing Loki around like a ragdoll

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.830
in 2012's "The Avengers."

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:18.490
She-Hulk is still a rookie contender who doesn't
seem interested in fighting anyone outside

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:19.720
of the courtroom.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:24.819
Still, in her first real test against Titania
in "She-Hulk: Attorney at Law," she wins easily.

00:03:24.819 --> 00:03:30.550
If it weren't for the largely overlooked early
MCU entry "The Incredible Hulk," starring

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:35.914
Edward Norton in the lead role instead of
Mark Ruffalo, the Hulks would have near-equal records.

00:03:35.999 --> 00:03:41.270
There is no argument that Bruce Banner is
one of the most intelligent Marvel characters.

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:47.830
A renowned scientist, he casually mentions
to Thor that he has seven PhDs during "Thor: Ragnarok."

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:53.220
Beyond his education, Banner has been an integral
partner to Tony Stark during multiple "Avengers"

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:59.000
movies, assisting in the construction of Ultron
and the time machine utilized in "Avengers: Endgame."

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.610
It's not just his post-transformation muscles
that are huge, he arguably has the biggest

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.609
brain in the whole MCU.

00:04:05.609 --> 00:04:09.728
"Well, if he can do that, he could achieve
heavy ion fusion on any reactor on the planet."

00:04:09.728 --> 00:04:11.887
"Finally, someone who speaks English."

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:14.240
"Is that what just happened?"

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:18.180
However, as Jennifer Walters states early
in "She-Hulk: Attorney at Law," Banner is

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:20.689
"not the only genius in the family."

00:04:20.689 --> 00:04:25.520
A highly competent lawyer, Walters may not
have the credentials that her cousin boasts,

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:30.500
but she knows the law like the back of her
big green hand and can more than hold her

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.050
own in a courtroom.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:36.509
Walters consistently takes clever jabs at
Banner and his alter-ego, proving that her

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:38.740
wit is a match for his.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:43.909
As her MCU series proves, She-Hulk often comes
out on top when arguing with her cousin.

00:04:44.091 --> 00:04:49.830
A significant factor that deserves consideration
is who a combatant has in their corner.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:53.659
Iron Man would have never beaten Thanos without
the help of the Avengers.

00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:57.960
Spider-Man could not have defeated Norman
Osborn without…Spider-Man.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.599
And even a Hulk needs backup once in a while.

00:05:00.599 --> 00:05:05.240
When it comes to Hulk versus She-Hulk, it's
doubtful that any MCU heroes would put themselves

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.800
in the middle of a family dispute.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:10.080
However, a good ally is always worth having
in your corner.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:15.159
In the comics, She-Hulk easily wins the friendship
round, being the ally and resident attorney

00:05:15.159 --> 00:05:19.819
of many Marvel heroes, including the Fantastic
Four and Captain Marvel.

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:24.960
Meanwhile, Hulk has been on the wrong side
of so many heroes that the Illuminati exiled

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.210
him from Earth.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:30.589
It's still early in She-Hulk's MCU career,
but it should be easy for her to make some

00:05:30.589 --> 00:05:32.069
superhero friends quickly.

00:05:32.069 --> 00:05:38.259
It is already confirmed that characters such
as Wong and Daredevil will appear in "She-Hulk: Attorney at Law."

00:05:38.259 --> 00:05:41.919
Meanwhile, the MCU version of Hulk has been
a staple of the Avengers line-up since the

00:05:41.919 --> 00:05:44.131
inaugural film in 2012.

00:05:44.131 --> 00:05:47.999
While trying to decide who would win in a
fight between She-Hulk and Hulk, it's worth

00:05:47.999 --> 00:05:52.300
looking at how a battle between Jennifer Walters
and Bruce Banner would pan out.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:55.339
Hulk in human form is not much of a combatant.

00:05:55.339 --> 00:06:00.099
Unlike other original Avengers, Banner never
gained hand-to-hand combat training and is

00:06:00.099 --> 00:06:02.159
often portrayed as a little timid.

00:06:02.159 --> 00:06:06.119
Sure, he impressively defeated Cull Obsidian
during "Avengers: Infinity War," but that

00:06:06.119 --> 00:06:10.029
fight would not have lasted very long without
Tony Stark's Hulkbuster outfit.

00:06:10.029 --> 00:06:13.710
Keeping things equal, Jennifer Walters is
not a highly trained combatant.

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:16.460
She's a successful lawyer dedicated to her
career.

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:20.749
Still, she's much more confident than her
meek scientist cousin.

00:06:20.749 --> 00:06:24.740
Based on the relationship showcased in "She-Hulk:
Attorney at Law," we suspect that Walters

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:29.490
regularly came out on top during childhood
familial roughhousing.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:33.210
And if the two were to fight without their
hulking abilities, there's reason to believe

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:34.970
that Walters would take the win.

00:06:35.308 --> 00:06:41.130
If the influx of superhero shows and movies
has proven anything, it's that you need someone

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:44.129
on your super team who packs a mighty punch.

00:06:44.129 --> 00:06:47.710
In the comics, a version of the Hulk has often
been part of the Avengers line-up.

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:49.819
In fact, he was part of the very first line-up.

00:06:49.819 --> 00:06:55.319
However, deciding who to recruit becomes difficult
when choosing between a raging giant beast

00:06:55.319 --> 00:06:57.360
and a composed powerhouse.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:03.339
In the case of Hulk, he is as strong as they
come and can take on some of the biggest challenges.

00:07:03.339 --> 00:07:07.490
Unfortunately, his penchant for flying off
the handle and causing more destruction than

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:10.830
good can become more of a burden than anything
else.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:15.719
Conversely, She-Hulk is a woman who keeps
her composure, most of the time, at least,

00:07:15.719 --> 00:07:19.860
and she can deliver blows of near-equal strength
to her powerful cousin.

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:24.699
Plus, Jennifer Walters has the added bonus
of being an established lawyer.

00:07:24.699 --> 00:07:28.729
While it is always nice to have a physicist
around, having someone who can take care of

00:07:28.729 --> 00:07:31.919
legal business in your squad certainly sounds
more promising.

00:07:31.919 --> 00:07:36.939
Both Hulk and She-Hulk have been part of the
Marvel collection for decades.

00:07:36.939 --> 00:07:40.889
She-Hulk first appeared in 1980 with her self-titled
comic book.

00:07:40.889 --> 00:07:46.219
Her relation to Bruce Banner helped her quickly
befriend many superheroes and she soon became

00:07:46.219 --> 00:07:50.490
a member of teams like the Fantastic Four,
the Avengers, and the Defenders.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:55.520
She-Hulk became a fan favorite thanks to her
comedy stylings that often featured her breaking

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:58.089
the fourth wall, long before Deadpool made
it cool.

00:07:58.089 --> 00:08:02.849
And in the early '90s, there was almost a
She-Hulk movie starring Brigitte Nielsen,

00:08:02.849 --> 00:08:06.080
as well as a couple of proposed television
shows.

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:11.939
Alternatively, Hulk was first introduced in
1962 and has remained a shining part of the

00:08:11.939 --> 00:08:13.550
Marvel roster since.

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:16.819
The character has become one of the most popular
superheroes globally.

00:08:16.819 --> 00:08:22.119
While the word "hulk" predates the Marvel
comics, it has become part of the English

00:08:22.119 --> 00:08:26.639
lexicon for someone losing control of their
temper, or "hulking out."

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:32.620
Spawning multiple comic titles, TV shows,
movies, video games, and plenty of other merchandise,

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:37.610
the original comic series "The Incredible
Hulk" has hundreds of issues.

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:43.459
While She-Hulk has some clout, she will always
be a variant of the original and may never

00:08:43.459 --> 00:08:45.792
reach the same level of popularity.

00:08:45.792 --> 00:08:52.279
In a fight between She-Hulk and Hulk, this
is the ultimate question: what is more powerful,

00:08:52.279 --> 00:08:55.250
pure anger or self-control?

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:58.860
It's this factor that differentiates the two
combatants.

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:01.670
Hulk is a synonym for rage.

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:08.649
It is his anger that not only triggers his
monstrous transformation but fuels him during battle.

00:09:08.649 --> 00:09:14.350
Not often explored in the MCU, Hulk's strength
is basically limitless, as the angrier he

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:16.548
is, the stronger he gets.

00:09:16.548 --> 00:09:19.337
"I know, I'm sorry, I just get so angry all
the time.

00:09:19.337 --> 00:09:20.337
Hulk always…

00:09:20.337 --> 00:09:21.668
Hulk always angry."

00:09:21.668 --> 00:09:27.720
On the other hand, She-Hulk has similar capabilities,
and her rage can cause her to become more dangerous.

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:32.279
However, the fact that Jennifer Walters has
more control over her alter ego arguably makes

00:09:32.279 --> 00:09:34.190
her a more formidable warrior.

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:38.329
As is pointed out during the first episode
of "She-Hulk: Attorney at Law," being a woman

00:09:38.329 --> 00:09:43.551
probably puts Walters leagues ahead of Banner
in the self-control department.

00:09:43.551 --> 00:09:45.937
"Triggers are anger and fear."

00:09:45.937 --> 00:09:48.336
"Those are like the baseline of any woman just existing."

00:09:48.336 --> 00:09:55.279
Where Hulk can fly off the handle and become
an unstoppable beast with near-unparalleled

00:09:55.279 --> 00:10:00.970
strength, She-Hulk has the patience and capability
to remain at the steering wheel.

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:06.620
Of course, she can also become a total rage
monster, but she has more choice in the matter.

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:11.470
Being able to maintain a cool head in a fight
against her rash and unruly cousin might just

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:13.089
be the deciding factor.

00:10:13.089 --> 00:10:21.009
Inarguably, one of the best toe-to-toe throwdowns
in the history of the MCU is Hulk versus Thanos

00:10:21.009 --> 00:10:23.009
in "Avengers: Infinity War."

00:10:23.009 --> 00:10:28.459
The fight highlighted just how powerful the
purple foe was while causing such damage to

00:10:28.459 --> 00:10:33.769
Hulk's ego that it took years for the mean,
green fighting machine to recuperate.

00:10:33.769 --> 00:10:38.779
That's why Bruce Banner had to use the Hulkbuster
armor to fight Cull Obsidian later in the movie.

00:10:38.779 --> 00:10:40.449
The Hulk refused to surface.

00:10:40.449 --> 00:10:44.630
But what if it had been She-Hulk aboard that
Asgardian ship as opposed to her cousin?

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:47.100
Would the result have been any different?

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:51.750
As seen in "Avengers: Endgame," female heroes
have fared much better than their male counterparts

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.170
when facing Thanos.

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:57.500
Scarlet Witch and Captain Marvel both held
their own against The Mad Titan.

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:02.529
Just like her cousin, She-Hulk would have
no doubt managed to get in some strong blows

00:11:02.529 --> 00:11:04.519
using the element of surprise.

00:11:04.519 --> 00:11:09.520
Unfortunately, Thanos is just too powerful
to be defeated by any one Avenger alone.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:13.149
Walters would have likely suffered the same
dreadful beating the Hulk took, although she

00:11:13.149 --> 00:11:16.790
may have been aware enough to avoid the one-on-one
fight altogether.

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:21.379
The real question should be: Would She-Hulk
have been capable of donning the Infinity

00:11:21.379 --> 00:11:27.690
Gauntlet and performing the same snap her
cousin did, bringing back half of the universe's occupants?

00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:32.029
She has the blood of the Hulk pumping through
her veins, so there's nothing to say that

00:11:32.029 --> 00:11:33.879
she couldn't withstand such a thing.

00:11:34.879 --> 00:11:40.910
Hulk versus She-Hulk would no doubt be a battle
for the ages, a real drop-down drag out of

00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:43.250
a fight that nobody would forget in a hurry.

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:50.223
The hits and destruction would probably resemble
the intense bout between Hulk and Thor in "Thor: Ragnarok."

00:11:50.223 --> 00:11:54.389
However, it's safe to say that this fight
would be much more personal.

00:11:54.389 --> 00:11:59.079
Whatever caused these combatants to throw
blows would no longer matter in the heat of

00:11:59.079 --> 00:12:03.800
the moment, as each would want to prove that
they are the strongest Hulk there is.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:08.500
She-Hulk would use her wits, her speed, and
her mobility to gain a strategic advantage

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:10.389
over her enormous cousin.

00:12:10.389 --> 00:12:16.130
Her more agile frame would allow her to dodge
the Hulk's powerful but easily telegraphed attacks.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:21.940
Still, it only takes one of those blows to
land, and the longer the fight went on, the

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:25.850
angrier, and therefore stronger, the Hulk
would become.

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:31.290
While his blows would be slower and fewer,
they would land much harder.

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:35.709
On top of that, Bruce Banner's alter ego surely
remembers the embarrassment served to him

00:12:35.709 --> 00:12:37.220
at the hands of Thanos.

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:42.610
The Hulk would not want to lose another big
fight, especially to his newcomer cousin.

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:46.734
As impressive as She-Hulk is she would have
a hard time keeping the Hulk down.

